      "raw": "Well done, that's a very well written description/example of the character generation process for a new player to look at.  If you plan on continuing to use that tumbler blog for Sentinels output do you want me to add a link to it over my [SCRPG resources page](https://villainyunpublished.blogspot.com/2024/05/other-sentinel-comics-rpg-online.html)?  Certainly merits as much of a signal boost as I can provide it.\n\nMinor correction, though:\n\n> Exclusive means that if you use it you can only use it, it won't stack with anything else.\n\nExclusive mods won't stack with other exclusives, so you can only use one per roll.  They can be combined with non-exclusives to your heart's content.  Usually that means you can't apply multiple persistent mods (which are almost always exclusive as well) but it also prevents you from using more than one Hero Point bonus at a time (which are exclusive, but **not** persistent).\n\nThe idea of a bow that can shoot snakes that is also a snake that you could use as a whip or (stiffened, I suppose, and biting with the snake head) as a fighting staff is very original.  Clever.  :)",
